  "title": "Neuma",
  "description": "Neuma is a multimodal neuromarketing dataset from 42 participants who browsed supermarket advertising brochures and selected the products they intended to buy. It combines EEG, eye tracking, questionnaire responses (demographic, profiling and product-related) and computer mouse data. The dataset supports research on consumer behavior and decision-making.",
  "methods_description": "Participants viewed a series of supermarket brochures containing various products and were instructed to select the products they intended to buy. EEG, eye tracking and computer mouse data were recorded during the task, and questionnaires were collected.",
